# Example /etc/hosts lines for stable Spark0..Spark3 name resolution.
#
# Copy to (append on each Spark, human-run):
#   /etc/hosts
#
# Use this only if you are NOT relying on mDNS (`*.local`) and you have a stable
# wired subnet. Adjust IPs to match your actual cabling + static leases.
#
# Suggested convention:
#   spark0 = 10.0.0.2
#   spark1 = 10.0.0.3
#   spark2 = 10.0.0.4
#   spark3 = 10.0.0.5
#
# If you pin /etc/hosts, update DS4_MASTER_ADDR / DS4_RING_HOSTS / DS4_PEER_HOST
# in `/etc/ds4/ds4-*.env` to match the pinned hostnames.
10.0.0.2 spark0
10.0.0.3 spark1
10.0.0.4 spark2
10.0.0.5 spark3

